Package: gfx906-rccl-topology
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.8), systemd
Suggests: resize-amdgpu-bars
Description: RCCL topology for the XGMI ring of gfx906 GPUs, regenerated at boot
 Writes the RCCL/NCCL topology file (NCCL_TOPO_FILE) for the XGMI links of
 AMD gfx906 GPUs from sysfs on every boot, so PCI renumbering (cards added
 or moved, PCIe switch pools changing) needs no manual edit, and points
 every RCCL process at it through /etc/rccl.conf.
 .
 On the Mac Pro 7,1 with two Radeon Pro Vega II Duo modules and the bridge,
 the XGMI hop table the firmware reports swaps the two bridge links; the
 generated topology has the physical ring instead (all-reduce bus bandwidth
 34 instead of 25 GB/s on four dies). Other gfx906 layouts get the
 firmware's links; other GPU families get no file.
